{% doc %}
  Article Card

  Renders the shared blog article card used by the blog listing and featured-blogs. The article image
  fills the card behind a gradient wash, with a category badge at the top and the title, date and
  read affordance at the bottom. Badge text and colours come from article metafields; the whole card
  is clickable via a stretched link on the title.

  @param {article} article - Article object (required)
  @param {string} read_label - Text for the read affordance, supplied by the calling section (required)

  All styling is Tailwind. Three utilities are load-bearing and easy to remove by accident:

  isolate on the root, with -z-20 on the image and -z-10 on the gradient — this keeps the ROOT as the
  containing block for the title's ::after, so the stretched link covers the whole card including its
  padding. Giving the content layer position: relative (the obvious way to stack it above the image)
  would make that layer the containing block instead, silently shrinking the click target to exclude
  the padding. isolate stops the negative indices painting behind an ancestor's background.

  Padding lives on the content layer, never the root — an absolutely positioned child resolves
  inset-0 against its ancestor's padding box, so padding on the root would inset the image and
  gradient and leave a visible frame.

  tracking-normal on the root — base.css sets body { letter-spacing: 0.01em }, which computes against
  the body's 16px and inherits as a flat 0.16px into every child regardless of its own size. The
  design specifies -0.16px on the title, so the root resets it and the type tokens override again.

  The read affordance is a span, never an anchor — it sits under the stretched ::after and is purely
  visual, which is what keeps this card to a single anchor.

  @example
  {% render 'article-card', article: article, read_label: section.settings.blog_read_label %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign article = article | default: blank

  unless article != blank
    break
  endunless

  assign badge_label = article.metafields.custom.category_label.value
  assign badge_background = article.metafields.custom.category_background_color.value
  assign badge_foreground = article.metafields.custom.category_text_color.value
  assign article_read_time = article.metafields.custom.read_time.value
  assign article_date = article.published_at | date: '%b %d'
  assign article_image_alt = article.image.alt | default: article.title

  if badge_background == blank
    assign badge_background = 'rgb(var(--color-green-secondary))'
  endif

  if badge_foreground == blank
    assign badge_foreground = '#FFFFFF'
  endif
-%}

<article class="article-card group relative isolate flex flex-col overflow-hidden aspect-[180/249] tracking-normal rounded-xl border border-[#A3A3A380] lg:aspect-[318/420] lg:rounded-[20px]">
  {%- if article.image != blank -%}
    <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-20">
      {%- render 'image',
        image: article.image,
        alt: article_image_alt,
        class_name: 'h-full w-full object-cover',
        base_width: 640,
        mobile_width: 400,
        breakpoint: 1024,
        lazy: true,
        decoding: 'async'
      -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-10 bg-gradient-to-b from-foreground/0 to-foreground"></div>

  <div class="flex flex-col justify-end h-full p-2.5 lg:p-5">
    {%- if badge_label != blank -%}
      <span
        class="self-start mb-auto px-2.5 py-1 whitespace-nowrap font-secondary text-[10px] font-medium leading-[15px] text-[color:var(--article-card-badge-fg)] bg-[color:var(--article-card-badge-bg)] rounded-md lg:px-3.5 lg:py-1.5 lg:text-label-sm lg:rounded-[10px]"
        style="--article-card-badge-bg: {{ badge_background | escape }}; --article-card-badge-fg: {{ badge_foreground | escape }};"
      >
        {{ badge_label | escape }}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-[5px]">
      <h3>
        <a
          href="{{ article.url }}"
          class="line-clamp-2 font-primary text-[14px] font-medium leading-[21px] tracking-[-0.16px] text-white after:absolute after:inset-0 lg:line-clamp-1 lg:text-[18px] lg:leading-[27px]"
        >
          {{ article.title | escape }}
        </a>
      </h3>

      {%- comment -%} Never transform the title's ancestors — that would make them the ::after containing block {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 transition-transform duration-300 lg:gap-3.5 [@media(hover:hover)]:group-hover:-translate-y-0.5">
        <p class="font-secondary text-body text-[#E5E5E5] lg:text-body-d">{{ article_date }}{% if article_read_time != blank %} &middot; {{ article_read_time | escape }}{% endif %}</p>

        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5 font-secondary text-[14px] font-semibold leading-[21px] text-white lg:text-label-lg">
          {{ read_label | escape }}
          {%- render 'icon-arrow-right',
            class: 'transition-transform duration-300 [@media(hover:hover)]:group-hover:translate-x-1'
          -%}
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
